{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>All the gold that was made, etc.</b> One needs to know the precise referent of the verse: where is its place? And if its saying ״twenty-nine kikkar״ is [already stated], if so, why did it return to say <b>And the gold was</b>, etc.? Perhaps, however, the precise referent of the verse is <b>in all the work of the sanctuary</b>, and the intention of the verse is to say that all the gold made for the work was not diminished, nor misused, nor was anything stolen from it, but everything entered into all the work of the sanctuary. And by this he cleared the craftsmen who worked on the labor of suspicion." "<b>Further,</b> it intends to inform of miracles that were performed with the gold of the Tabernacle. For it is a known thing that when a man makes a vessel of gold or of other metals, in any case it diminishes from the measure of the weight of the gold from which the vessel was made, and the vessel will not stand at its original weight, due to the subdivision and the processes of its crafting — and how much more so when the work involves much subdivision and fine parts, where it is obvious that it will diminish proportionately. Furthermore, when a man prepares the materials for the work — as, for example, warp and woof to weave a fabric of gold threads to make the work from them — it is impossible that he will calculate precisely with the prepared materials, neither less nor more. And here the verse informs that a miracle was performed, such that all the gold made for the work was <b>in all the work of the sanctuary.</b> From the word <b>kol</b> (all) He informed you that nothing was diminished by the processes of the work as mentioned, and from the word <b>ha-asui</b> (that was made) He noted as well that none of the materials prepared for the work was left over from it as waste, but everything entered into all the work of the sanctuary. And He was precise to say <b>be-chol</b> (in all) and did not say ״in the work of the sanctuary״ — He intended to say as well that what was made sufficed for everything. And this is the essence of the miracle, for without this there is no miracle in the fact that nothing was left over, for it is possible that he measured an amount that would certainly leave nothing over. Rather, the miracle was recognized only in the proportionality — that nothing was left over and nothing was lacking."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:15.160094697Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}